I committed it as 51031de7 (Part of #982). Four verbs that take no arguments now refuse a stray one, and a fifth refuses a bad count. memories stays as it was on purpose.

What changed (src/dispatch_sub.rs):
• yoyo status zzz, version zzz, permissions zzz and security zzz now print unexpected argument 'zzz' for \yoyo <verb>\ and a usage line on stderr, print nothing on stdout, and exit 2. Before, they printed their normal output and exited 0.
• Flags still work: version -v --provider x --model y and permissions --trust-project --yes. Only positional words count as stray; flags, and the value after a flag that takes one, are skipped.
• `evolution` takes one optional number. Before, evolution zzz quietly fell back to 10. Now evolution zzz and evolution 5 6 exit 2, and evolution 5 still runs. This only applies from the shell; /evolution zzz inside a session is unchanged.
• `memories` is not changed. memories zzz is a real search for "zzz", so 0 is correct. The commit title still lists it because I used the title as given; the commit body says it wasn't changed.

Other tools disagree: cargo version zzz and rustup show zzz exit 1 with an error, while git version zzz, gh version zzz and rustc --version zzz ignore it and exit 0. So refusing was my call. I used exit 2 because yoyo's other usage errors already exit 2.

Checks: The new test is zero_arg_verbs_refuse_a_stray_argument_with_exit_two in tests/integration.rs. It runs the real binary in a temp dir and checks six refused cases, six bare-verb and flag cases that must still succeed, and that evolution 5 gets past the refusal. As a sanity check, I removed the refusal from status: the test failed on ["status","zzz"], and passed again once I put it back. fmt, clippy (-D warnings), build and the full test suite all pass. I raised the size limit for dispatch_sub.rs in tests/module_size.rs from 2457 to 2503 lines, and added one sentence about this to docs/src/usage/commands.md.

Comment on #982: I posted one comment with the before/after table, the comparison with other tools, and what's left. The first version wrongly listed docs zzz as ignoring its argument, but zzz is a real crate on docs.rs, so it was working correctly. I fixed that in the comment and in the commit message (amended before any push, which is why the sha changed), and the comment now points at 51031de7.

Still open in this class: doctor zzz, help zzz, init zzz and update zzz still ignore the stray argument and exit 0, and init zzz still writes a YOYO.md file. health zzz exits 1, but only because there's no project; it ignores the argument too.
